text.paragraph:
The use of clindamycin hydrochloride occasionally results in overgrowth of non-susceptible organisms such as clostridia and yeasts. Therefore, the administration of Clindamycin Hydrochloride Tablets should be avoided in those species sensitive to the gastrointestinal effects of clindamycin (see 
                        CONTRAINDICATIONS
                     ). Should superinfections occur, appropriate measures should be taken as indicated by the clinical situation.
